Execution flow

1. User creates monitor in UI
2. API validates request
3. Monitor metadata saved in Aurora
4. Script stored in Git and packaged into S3
5. Scheduler finds monitor when due
6. Scheduler creates execution record
7. Scheduler writes idempotency lock in DynamoDB
8. Scheduler sends message to SQS
9. Job Manager polls SQS
10. Job Manager fetches config from Aurora
11. Job Manager fetches script from S3
12. Job Manager fetches secrets from AWS Secrets Manager
13. k6 runs the check
14. Result Processor stores result in Aurora
15. Metrics emitted to Prometheus
16. Screenshots/logs/HAR uploaded to S3
17. DynamoDB updated with latest status
18. Alert Engine evaluates rule
19. Notification sent to PagerDuty/Slack/Email/ServiceNow



